<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-22">22 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Rome defeats Macedon at Pydna</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a>'s legions broke the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> of King Perseus. The Antigonid kingdom was abolished, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> became the dominant power in the Greek world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pydna">Battle of Pydna</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Pydna was fought on 22 June 168 BCE near Pydna in Macedonia, where a Roman army under Lucius Aemilius Paullus defeated King Perseus of Macedon.</p></div></li></ol></section>
